  "research": "Supine (head toward +Y). 12 Nov fix: (1) the dumbbell never showed because its handle axis [0,0,1] was parallel to the torso 'up' the prop frame is built from (frame_from) -> zero-size matrix; now the handle lies along the body turned 30 deg in the chest plane (axis [0.5,0.013,0.866], perpendicular to the forearm, so the wrist stays straight). (2) hands moved from defaults into both poses (the bake keys the arm bones only when a POSE has arm angles). (3) left hand grips the handle centre at torso (0.07,0.25,-0.17): plates (r 0.088) rest on the chest skin (~0.15 in front of the shoulder line) instead of 4 cm inside it; FK: upper arm 0.269 + forearm-to-grip 0.33 -> elbow 112, elbow tucked by the ribs ~3.5 cm off the floor. Right hand (no prop) at torso (-0.085,0.25,-0.17): 0.134 m from the handle line, beside the lower plate (clear by ~8 mm), so both hands are on the weight. (4) back floated ~3 cm (root 0.11; toe_touch_crunch measured the upper back 0.080 below the pelvis joint): root 0.10 and rot X -92 (head end 2 deg down) -> upper back ~0.006, buttocks unmeasured (<= 0.111 below the joint): read lowest_body_z and the side view, then shift root z by it. End curl 3+8+10+10+9 = 40 deg (was 32: start and end looked alike), pelvis and feet unchanged. Ankle (0.12,-0.627,0.074). Sources S1 Escamilla 2006, S2 Moraes 2009, S3 Oliva-Lozano 2020. Facts: research/weighted_crunch.json."
